==German==
{{wikipedia|lang=de}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈjeːmən/|/ˈjɛmən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Jemen.ogg|Audio}}

===Proper noun===
{{de-proper noun|m,-:s,-.article}} ''or'' {{de-proper noun|n,s}}

# {{place|de|country|r/Western Asia|t=Yemen}}

====Usage notes====
* The word is sometimes used without a definite article (as in English): {{m|de||Jemen, in Jemen}}. In this case, the genitive is always {{m|de||Jemens}}; for example {{m|de||Jemens Hauptstadt|t=Yemen’s capital}}.
* More commonly, however, the masculine definite article is used with the name: {{m|de||der Jemen, im Jemen}}. In this case, the genitive is {{m|de||des Jemen}} or less often {{m|de||des Jemens}}; thus {{m|de||die Hauptstadt des Jemen(s)|t=the capital of Yemen}}.
* The plural form refers to North Yemen ({{m|de|Nordjemen}}) and South Yemen ({{m|de|Südjemen}}); for example {{m|de||die beiden Jemen|t=the two Yemen[s]}}.

====Related terms====
* {{l|de|Jemenit}}
* {{l|de|jemenitisch}}
* {{l|de|Nordjemen}}
* {{l|de|Südjemen}}

